{"id":2948,"path":"/grammar-points/a2/present-perfect/","parentId":542,"order":90,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a2","depth":3,"title":"Present perfect: Form and use","seo":{"title":"Present perfect: Form and use - Test-English","description":"Learn the present perfect form and use in this A2 Pre-intermediate grammar lesson. Clear rules, charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/A2%E2%80%93Present-perfect.png"},"modified":"2026-02-19T17:24:48","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose <em>for</em> or&nbsp;<em>since</em> to complete the following present perfect sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"355\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the most appropriate forms to complete the following present perfect sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"356\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Write sentences with the words below using the present perfect tense.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"357\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 4</h3> <h5>Complete the sentences using the present perfect form of the verbs in brackets.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"358\"></div>"],"explanation":"<h2>Present perfect: Form</h2> <p>We form the present perfect tense with the verb <strong>have</strong> and the past participle of the verb. The past participle is the same as the past simple (<strong>-ed</strong>) for regular verbs. For irregular verbs, it’s the form in the 3rd column.<br> <br> <img class=\"alignleft size-full wp-image-11260\" src=\"/media/uploads/Present-perfect-form_new.png\" alt=\"Present perfect – form\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h2>Present perfect: Use</h2> <p>We normally use the present perfect to talk about past events that have a connection with the present, for example, news or past experiences. We can also use the present perfect to talk about situations that started in the past but which are still true in the present. Check the grammar chart below:<br> <br> <img class=\"alignleft size-full wp-image-11261\" src=\"/media/uploads/Present-perfect-use_new.png\" alt=\"Present perfect – use\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h3>Recent events and news</h3> <p>We use the present perfect to talk about recent events or news. We don’t say when these events happened.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I’<span><strong>ve passed</strong></span> the test!</em></li> <li><em>She’<strong><span>s broken</span></strong> her arm.</em></li> <li><em>The president <strong><span>has travelled</span></strong> to Cuba.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h4>⇒ Just, yet, already</h4> <p>We often use the present perfect with the words <strong>just,</strong> <a href=\"/grammar-points/b1-b2/already-still-yet-whats-the-difference/\"><strong>yet, already</strong></a>.<br> <br> We use <strong>just</strong> in (+) sentences to say that something happened very recently (like minutes ago).</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I’<span><strong>ve just seen</strong></span> Peter in the street.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>He looks happy because he’<strong><span>s just got married</span></strong>.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>yet</strong> in (-) and (?) sentences. We put it at the end of the sentence.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Have</strong></span> you <span><strong>washed</strong></span> the dishes <span><strong>yet</strong></span>?</em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>haven’t</strong></span> <strong><span>called</span></strong> him <span><strong>yet</strong></span>.</em></li> <li><em>She <span><strong>hasn’t arrived yet</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>already </strong>in<strong>&nbsp;</strong>(+) sentences to say that something happened before now (usually earlier than we expected).</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I <span><strong>have already finished</strong></span>.</em></li> <li><em>We <span><strong>have already arrived</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h3>Life experiences</h3> <p>We often use the present perfect to talk about past experiences in our lives. We don’t say when these experiences happened.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I’<span><strong>ve run</strong></span> the Boston Marathon twice.</em></li> <li><em>She’<span><strong>s</strong></span> never <span><strong>been</strong></span> on a cruise.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I’<span><strong>ve been</strong> </span>here before.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h4>⇒ <a href=\"/grammar-points/shorts/never-vs-ever-grammar-shorts/\">Never, ever</a>, before</h4> <p>When we ask about someone’s life experiences, we often use the word&nbsp;<strong>ever</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Have</strong></span> you <span><strong>ever</strong> <strong>read</strong></span> this book?</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Have</strong></span> you <span><strong>ever</strong></span> <span><strong>been</strong></span> to India?</em></li> </ul> <p>When we talk about life experiences, we often use the words <strong>never</strong> or <strong>before</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>She <span><strong>has never been</strong></span> late.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I think I <span><strong>have seen</strong></span> this film <span><strong>before</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h3>Unfinished actions</h3> <h4>⇒ How long, for, since</h4> <p>We use the present perfect with the words <strong>how long</strong>,&nbsp;<a href=\"/grammar-points/b1/for-since-from-difference/\"><strong>for</strong>, <strong>since</strong></a>&nbsp;to talk about actions or situations that started in the past and still continue or are still true now.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I’<span><strong>ve lived</strong></span> in Oslo <strong><span>since</span></strong> I was born.</em> (=I was born in Oslo and I still live in Oslo)</li> <li><em>They <span><strong>have been</strong></span> married <span><strong>for</strong></span> 25 years.</em> (=They got married 25 years ago and they are still married)</li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>how long</strong> in questions to ask about the duration of an action or situation.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>How long</strong> <strong>has</strong></span> she <span><strong>been</strong></span> a teacher?</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>How long</strong> <strong>has</strong></span> she <span><strong>had</strong></span> her car?</em></li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>for</strong> + a period of time, e.g. <strong>for</strong> two weeks, <strong>for</strong> ten years, <strong>for</strong> ten days, <strong>for</strong> a few hours, etc.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>We’<span><strong>ve been</strong></span> here <span><strong>for</strong></span> a few hours.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>They’<span><strong>ve been</strong></span> married <span><strong>for</strong></span> 10 years.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>since</strong> + a moment in the past (the beginning of a period of time), e.g. <strong>since</strong> I was born, <strong>since</strong> 10 o’clock, <strong>since</strong> last Wednesday, etc.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>We’<span><strong>ve been</strong></span> here <span><strong>since</strong></span> 4 o’clock.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>They’<span><strong>ve been</strong></span> married <span><strong>since</strong></span> 2010.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h2>Be careful with these common mistakes!</h2> <p>We use the present perfect, and not the present simple for actions or situations that started in the past and are still true now.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>We<span><strong>&nbsp;<span>are</span></strong></span> friends since first grade</em>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>We’<span><strong>ve been</strong></span> friends since first grade</em>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> </ul> <p>We use&nbsp;<strong>for…&nbsp;</strong>and NOT&nbsp;<strong>since…</strong><strong>ago</strong> to introduce a period of time.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><span><em>They’ve been married <span><strong>since 10 years ago</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></span><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><span><em>They’ve been married <span><strong>for 10 years</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></span><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":355,"questions":[{"id":3026,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I've had this car <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> years.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["since","for"]}]},{"id":3027,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We've known each other <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> we were in school.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["since","for"]}]},{"id":3028,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I haven't eaten anything <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> this morning. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["for","since"]}]},{"id":3029,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She hasn't slept <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> two days. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["for","since"]}]},{"id":3030,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I have wanted to be a writer <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> I was a child. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["for","since"]}]},{"id":3031,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We've been together <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> over ten years. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["since","for"]}]},{"id":3032,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I haven't seen John <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> last July. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["for","since"]}]},{"id":3033,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>It hasn't rained <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> a long time. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["since","for"]}]},{"id":3034,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She's worked in this bank <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> 25 years. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["since","for"]}]},{"id":3035,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She's worked in this bank <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> it first opened.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["for","since"]}]}]},{"id":356,"questions":[{"id":3036,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ to Rome?</div>","choices":[{"id":5218,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Have ever you been</span>"},{"id":5219,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Have you ever been</span>"},{"id":5220,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Have you been ever</span>"}]},{"id":3037,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Have you had lunch _____?</div>","choices":[{"id":5221,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>yet</span>"},{"id":5222,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>just</span>"},{"id":5223,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>already</span>"}]},{"id":3038,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I _____ the keys that I lost yet.</div>","choices":[{"id":5224,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>haven't find</span>"},{"id":5225,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>haven't finded</span>"},{"id":5226,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>haven't found</span>"}]},{"id":3039,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I _____ Peter since I was 5 years old.</div>","choices":[{"id":5227,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>know</span>"},{"id":5228,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>'ve known</span>"},{"id":5229,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>'ve knew</span>"}]},{"id":3040,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I _____ my pen. Can I use yours?</div>","choices":[{"id":5230,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>'ve losed</span>"},{"id":5231,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>lose</span>"},{"id":5232,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>have lost </span>"}]},{"id":3041,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>A: 'Where's Celine?' B: 'She ______.'</div>","choices":[{"id":5233,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>'s just left</span>"},{"id":5234,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>just has left </span>"},{"id":5235,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>has left just</span>"}]},{"id":3042,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I've been here _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":5236,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>since a week ago</span>"},{"id":5237,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>since a week</span>"},{"id":5238,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>for a week</span>"}]},{"id":3043,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We _____ insects before.</div>","choices":[{"id":5239,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>never have ate</span>"},{"id":5240,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>'ve never eaten</span>"},{"id":5241,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>never have eaten</span>"}]},{"id":3044,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We've known each other since we _____ children.</div>","choices":[{"id":5242,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>were</span>"},{"id":5243,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>have been </span>"},{"id":5244,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>are</span>"}]},{"id":3045,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ raining yet?</div>","choices":[{"id":5245,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Has it stop</span>"},{"id":5246,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Does it stopped</span>"},{"id":5247,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Has it stopped</span>"}]}]},{"id":357,"questions":[{"id":3046,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He/lose/his keys. <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3047,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I/have (not)/coffee this morning. <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3048,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She/never/lie/to us. <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3049,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>You/read/that newspaper/yet? <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3050,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We/be/to England/many times. <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3051,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Where/you/be? <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3052,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>David/win/the competition. <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3053,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>My son/break/his leg. <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3054,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I/never/see/her/before. <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3055,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They/write/a book. <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]},{"id":358,"questions":[{"id":3056,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (not have) breakfast yet. Would you like to have it with me?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3057,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (never/be) to the Himalayas, but I'd like to go. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3058,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (know) the truth since the beginning. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3059,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (buy) a very expensive car.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3060,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (just/get) married.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3061,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>What <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (you/do)?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3062,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (you/ever/work) abroad?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3063,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (already/find) a solution. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3064,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I think I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (see) this picture before. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3065,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (you/ever/meet) a celebrity?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}